ause pretty much all the things  that they changed in terms of what was  removed  and the streamlining and what the  changes were in sort of a sub we're all  working towards making it work better as  a film because a lot of what works about  the book is stuff that doesn't translate  the the the literary flow of a fairy  tale because it is written anyway to  evoke a fairy tale doesn't have a direct  translation and one of the point the  book doesn't really have a climax it  just kind of goes until it ends until  you know it reaches its ending where you  get your little and then this happened  then that and at the end but it doesn't  have it certainly doesn't have a  cinematic climax it arguably doesn't  really have a climax at all and a movie  get kind of need one and they do  manufacture one that said the film could  still stand to be streamlined a little  bit more than it is the movie runs over  two hours and I think there's probably  about 20 minutes that could have been  saved from it particularly from the tail  end and actually from the climax and I  am gonna get into a little bit of spies  I'm not gonna go into heavy detail here  but I mean if you haven't already seen  it what I'm about to describe as far as  the climax goes you know has to do with  what's happening to the end if you know  everyone's looking for the star what am  I allowed to describe is not really  spoiler it's a set up you should  appreciate so we're in a situation where  all interested parties the surviving  Prince's the witch and Tristan are all  converging on a vein and it's actually  building really amazingly as they're all  all coming together and like boy this is  really gonna come to a head but it  doesn't what happens is a vein gets  kidnapped by one of the people involved  taken somewhere else and then the others  have to go to this other place and we  have to we have to build a new head of  steam for a climax and it's really kind  of odd it built to a very organic  natural climax an